# Go

Match the packages already here. Stdlib first. Small files. Tests live next to the package (`foo_test.go`).

```go
// ❌ BAD — new assertion library, table helper framework
require.Equal(t, KindCar, a.Kind)

// ✅ GOOD — same style as parse_test.go
if a.Kind != KindCar {
    t.Fatalf("kind=%s", a.Kind)
}
```

- `gofmt` on edit. After non-trivial Go changes, run `make test`.
- Prefer `net/http` ServeMux patterns already in `internal/web`.
- Wrap errors at trust boundaries (`fmt.Errorf("…: %w", err)`). Do not swallow upsert/poll failures silently beyond existing `log.Printf` + continue.
- Leave one test that fails if the new logic breaks. Trivial one-liners need none.
